                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p142-q47-a-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Substitute successively and retain every earlier exclusion after simplification.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Write $D_n$ for the domain of the composition containing $n$ copies of $f$.\n\n$$f(x)=\\frac{1}{x+1}.$$\nThe denominator is nonzero when $x\\ne-1$, so\n$$D_1=\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{-1\\}.$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(f\\circ f)(x)&=\\frac{1}{1+\\frac{1}{x+1}}\\\\(f\\circ f)(x)&=\\frac{x+1}{x+2}.\\end{align*}$$\nRetain $x\\ne-1$ and also require $x\\ne-2$:\n$$D_2=\\mathbb R\\setminus\\{-1,-2\\}.$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(f\\circ f\\circ f)(x)&=\\frac{1}{1+\\frac{x+1}{x+2}}\\\\(f\\circ f\\circ f)(x)&=\\frac{x+2}{2x+3}.\\end{align*}$$\nRetain the exclusions in $D_2$ and also require $2x+3\\ne0$:\n$$D_3=\\mathbb R\\setminus\\left\\{-1,-2,-\\frac32\\right\\}.$$\n\n$$\\begin{align*}(f\\circ f\\circ f\\circ f)(x)&=\\frac{1}{1+\\frac{x+2}{2x+3}}\\\\(f\\circ f\\circ f\\circ f)(x)&=\\frac{2x+3}{3x+5}.\\end{align*}$$\nRetain the exclusions in $D_3$ and also require $3x+5\\ne0$:\n$$D_4=\\mathbb R\\setminus\\left\\{-1,-2,-\\frac32,-\\frac53\\right\\}.$$\n\nSimplifying a later expression does not restore an input excluded by an earlier composition.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 100
      },
      {
        "id": "p142-q47-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "As this composition continues, what pattern emerges in the domain of $f\\circ\\cdots\\circ f$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
