        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p142-q47-b-short-definition",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Let ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "F_1=F_2=1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "F_{k+2}=F_{k+1}+F_k",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " for ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "k\\ge1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ". For ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "n",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " copies of ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "f",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ",",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p142-q47-b-short-domain",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "D_n=\\mathbb R\\setminus\\left\\{-\\frac{F_{k+1}}{F_k}:1\\le k\\le n\\right\\}.",
                    "display": true
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p142-q47-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Retain all earlier exclusions; step ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "n",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " adds ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "-\\frac{F_{n+1}}{F_n}",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ". The denominator coefficients follow the Fibonacci recurrence.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Let $h_n$ be the composition containing $n$ copies of $f$. If its simplified rule is $h_n(x)=\\frac{P_n(x)}{Q_n(x)}$, then\n$$\\begin{align*}h_{n+1}(x)&=f(h_n(x))\\\\h_{n+1}(x)&=\\frac{1}{1+\\frac{P_n(x)}{Q_n(x)}}\\\\h_{n+1}(x)&=\\frac{Q_n(x)}{P_n(x)+Q_n(x)}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe new numerator is the previous denominator, and the new denominator is the sum of the previous numerator and denominator. Starting with $P_1(x)=1$ and $Q_1(x)=x+1$, the denominators are\n$$x+1,\\quad x+2,\\quad 2x+3,\\quad 3x+5,\\quad 5x+8,\\quad\\ldots.$$\nTheir coefficients follow the Fibonacci recurrence. Define\n$$F_1=F_2=1,\\qquad F_{k+2}=F_{k+1}+F_k\\quad(k\\ge1).$$\nThe denominator of the $n$th simplified rule is\n$$Q_n(x)=F_nx+F_{n+1}.$$\nIt vanishes at $x=-\\frac{F_{n+1}}{F_n}$. Each composition retains every earlier exclusion, so\n$$D_n=\\mathbb R\\setminus\\left\\{-\\frac{F_{k+1}}{F_k}:1\\le k\\le n\\right\\},\\qquad n\\ge1.$$\nThus the successive excluded inputs are $-1,-2,-\\frac32,-\\frac53,-\\frac85,\\ldots$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
